    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0273" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg199"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extract]</note>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Portman.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 20, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your two despatches, No. 65 and 66, dated
                    the 18th and 30th of November, 1865, respectively, have been received.</p>
                <pb facs="0274" n="200" xml:id="pg200"/>
                <p>Your proceedings, as therein narrated, appear to have been discreet, and are
                    approved. We await the details promised in your No. 66, of the late negotiations
                    at Osacca, and in the mean time I transmit enclosed<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d182-f1"/> a copy of our late correspondence on the subject with the
                    French government.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. L. C. Portman</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d182-f1" n="*" xml:id="d182-f1-content">
                <p>For enclosure see correspondence with United States minister to France.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
